# Registry block media (images & video)

Use this when a block needs bundled raster images (PNG, JPG, WebP) or video (MP4, WebM). Most blocks (navbars, SVG-only sections, etc.) do not need this.

## Where assets live

**Images**

```
public/images/blocks/<block-id>/
  hero-section-v8-bg.png
  avatar_1.png
```

**Video**

```
public/videos/blocks/<block-id>/
  screen-demo.mp4
```

Do not put images or videos inside `registry/new-york/blocks/<block-id>/`.

## Block code

Reference **local public paths** only — no CDN URLs, no URL-mapping helper:

```tsx
<Image src="/images/blocks/hero-section-v8/hero-section-v8-bg.png" alt="..." />
```

```tsx
<video
  src="/videos/blocks/macbook-pro-with-video/screen-demo.mp4"
  muted
  playsInline
  autoPlay
  loop
/>
```

```ts
const avatar = (filename: string) =>
  `/images/blocks/testimonials-section-v1/${filename}`
```

Prefer each block’s own folder (`public/videos/blocks/<this-block-id>/`). If two blocks share one file, keep a single copy on disk and declare that `registry:file` entry in **every** block that references it.

## registry.json

Declare every image and video so `shadcn add` installs code and assets in one step:

```json
{
  "path": "public/images/blocks/hero-section-v8/hero-section-v8-bg.png",
  "type": "registry:file",
  "target": "public/images/blocks/hero-section-v8/hero-section-v8-bg.png"
}
```

```json
{
  "path": "public/videos/blocks/macbook-pro-with-video/screen-demo.mp4",
  "type": "registry:file",
  "target": "public/videos/blocks/macbook-pro-with-video/screen-demo.mp4"
}
```

After adding or changing media: `pnpm registry:build`.

## Consumer swap

Installed assets land at the same paths under `public/images/blocks/<block-id>/` and `public/videos/blocks/<block-id>/`. Replace files in place to use custom media — no code changes unless filenames change.

## Do not

- Reference media with `https://uiception.com/images/...` or `https://uiception.com/videos/...` in block code
- Ship images or video via a post-install download script — bundle in `registry.json` `files`
- Omit `registry:file` entries when block code references `/images/blocks/<block-id>/` or `/videos/blocks/<block-id>/`
